From 9cf2f7e671ade10c7e785028d50d8131eed0fbf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:01:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] retain exact dashboard histories across task-only
 changes

Task-wide P2 marks currently discard immutable event histories even when only task content, runs, comments or neighbours changed. Compare the ordered typed SQLite scalars before reusing history reductions. Keep fresh task/run/graph/wake reads and reload changed events, including same-ID edits.

Proof: baseline-compatible RED on title-only reload. 29 consumer files: 525 tests green; added schema-rename control green separately. scripts/check --base origin/main green. Captured hub-board A/B: parent-equivalent 72.48ms, candidate 52.86ms, parent-repeat 65.85ms per content-edit GET (30 samples each), cold payload parity in all three. These fixture timings are not live CPU acceptance; 1.97% is only a theoretical zero-materialization floor.
